# Flow, host and pair state cases. A `scenario` line opens one: its own
# server port and client address. Each rule line under it starts with `>`
# (the rule reads what clients send to that port) or `<` (what the server
# sends back), then holds the rule's options. Each indented line is a packet:
# the second it is sent, `>` from a client or `<` from the server, optionally
# `cN` for the client port (c0 when absent), then the payload as a Suricata
# content string. make-flow-verdicts.py sends them to a real Suricata and
# records which rules alerted on each packet.

scenario a bit set by one rule is read by a later packet, in order only
> flowbits:set,auth; flowbits:noalert; content:"LOGIN";
> flowbits:isset,auth; content:"DATA";
  0 > "DATA"
  1 > "LOGIN"
  2 > "DATA"
  3 > c1 "DATA"

scenario a bit set by the client is read on the server's answer
> flowbits:set,req; content:"REQ";
< flowbits:isset,req; content:"RESP";
  0 < "RESP"
  1 > "REQ"
  2 < "RESP"

scenario a rule setting a bit runs before a rule reading it on one packet
> flowbits:isset,both; content:"AB";
> flowbits:set,both; content:"A";
  0 > "AB"
  1 > c1 "B"
  2 > c1 "AB"

scenario unset, toggle and isnotset
> flowbits:set,on; content:"SET";
> flowbits:unset,on; content:"CLEAR";
> flowbits:toggle,on; content:"FLIP";
> flowbits:isset,on; content:"ASK";
> flowbits:isnotset,on; content:"NOT";
  0 > "ASK NOT"
  1 > "SET"
  2 > "ASK NOT"
  3 > "CLEAR"
  4 > "ASK NOT"
  5 > "FLIP"
  6 > "ASK NOT"
  7 > "FLIP"
  8 > "ASK NOT"

scenario a test of a|b reads any of the names
> flowbits:set,b; flowbits:noalert; content:"SETB";
> flowbits:isset,a|b; content:"ANY";
> flowbits:isnotset,a|b; content:"NONE";
  0 > "ANY NONE"
  1 > "SETB"
  2 > "ANY NONE"

scenario a&b is one bit of that name
> flowbits:set,a; content:"SETA";
> flowbits:set,b; content:"SETB";
> flowbits:isset,a&b; content:"ALL";
> flowbits:isnotset,a&b; content:"NALL";
> flowbits:set,x|y; content:"SETXY";
> flowbits:isset,x; content:"ISX";
  0 > "SETA SETB"
  1 > "ALL NALL"
  2 > "SETXY"
  3 > "ISX"

scenario noalert alone still writes
> noalert; flowbits:set,quiet; content:"HUSH";
> flowbits:isset,quiet; content:"LOUD";
  0 > "HUSH"
  1 > "LOUD"

scenario a flowint counts packets
> flowint:hits,+,1; flowint:hits,>=,3; content:"HIT";
  0 > "HIT"
  1 > "HIT"
  2 > "HIT"
  3 > "HIT"
  4 > c1 "HIT"

scenario a flowint written by one rule is compared by another
> flowint:level,=,5; content:"SETL";
> flowint:level,+,2; content:"ADDL";
> flowint:level,==,7; content:"IS7";
> flowint:level,>,other; content:"VAR";
> flowint:level,isset; content:"HAS";
> flowint:unset_var,notset; content:"NOV";
  0 > "IS7 HAS NOV VAR"
  1 > "SETL"
  2 > "IS7"
  3 > "ADDL"
  4 > "IS7 HAS VAR"

scenario a flowint added by one rule and compared by another
> flowint:count,+,1; flowint:noalert_unused,notset; content:"INC";
> flowint:count,>=,2; content:"INC";
> flowint:count,<,other; content:"LESS";
> flowint:count,==,other; content:"SAME";
  0 > "INC"
  1 > "INC"
  2 > "INC LESS SAME"

scenario a flowint compared before it is added in one rule
> flowint:seen,>=,1; flowint:seen,+,1; content:"TWICE";
  0 > "TWICE"
  1 > "TWICE"
  2 > "TWICE"

scenario a flowint step before a failing content
> flowint:early,+,1; content:"NEVER";
> flowint:early,isset; content:"EARLY";
  0 > "EARLY"
  1 > "EARLY"

scenario a pair bit is seen from the other address of the pair
> xbits:set,pair,track ip_pair; content:"PSET";
< xbits:isset,pair,track ip_pair; content:"PGET";
  0 > "PSET"
  1 < c1 "PGET"

scenario a source bit lives on the address and expires
> xbits:set,seen,track ip_src,expire 10; xbits:noalert; content:"MARK";
> xbits:isset,seen,track ip_src; content:"CHECK";
  0 > "MARK"
  1 > c1 "CHECK"
  10 > c2 "CHECK"
  11 > c3 "CHECK"
  100 > "MARK"
  105 > "MARK"
  111 > c1 "CHECK"

scenario a destination bit is the server's address
> xbits:set,target,track ip_dst; content:"TSET";
< xbits:isset,target,track ip_src; content:"TGET";
> xbits:isset,target,track ip_src; content:"TSRC";
  0 > "TSET"
  1 < "TGET"
  2 > "TSRC"

scenario hostbits share the host's bits
> hostbits:set,host,src; content:"HSET";
< hostbits:isset,host,dst; content:"HGET";
< xbits:isset,host,track ip_dst; content:"XGET";
  0 > "HSET"
  1 < c1 "HGET XGET"

scenario a detection filter alerts past its count until its window closes
> detection_filter:track by_src, count 2, seconds 10; content:"FLOOD";
  0 > "FLOOD"
  1 > c1 "FLOOD"
  2 > c2 "FLOOD"
  3 > c3 "FLOOD"
  10 > "FLOOD"
  11 > "FLOOD"
  12 > "FLOOD"

scenario a pcre capture kept on the flow is read by a later packet of it
> pcre:"/user=(?P<flow_user>[a-z]+)/";
> flowvar:user,"bob"; content:"CHECK";
  0 > "user=bob"
  1 > "CHECK"
  2 > c1 "CHECK"

scenario a flow variable is compared whole or in part
> pcre:"/name=(?P<flow_name>[a-z]+)/";
> flowvar:name,"li"; content:"PART";
> flowvar:name,"alice"; content:"WHOLE";
> flowvar:name,"alicex"; content:"LONGER";
  0 > "name=alice"
  1 > "PART WHOLE LONGER"

scenario a capture named after the flags is kept as one named in the group
> pcre:"/id=([0-9]+)/,flow:ident";
> flowvar:ident,"42"; content:"IDCHK";
  0 > "id=42"
  1 > "IDCHK"

scenario a capture of a rule that does not match is not kept
> pcre:"/tok=(?P<flow_tok>[a-z]+)/"; content:"NEVER";
> flowvar:tok,"abc"; content:"TCHK";
  0 > "tok=abc"
  1 > "TCHK"

scenario a later capture replaces an earlier one
> pcre:"/v=(?P<flow_v>[a-z]+)/";
> flowvar:v,"one"; content:"VONE";
> flowvar:v,"two"; content:"VTWO";
  0 > "v=one"
  1 > "VONE VTWO"
  2 > "v=two"
  3 > "VONE VTWO"

scenario a packet variable lives on its packet only
> pcre:"/p=(?P<pkt_p>[a-z]+)/";
> pktvar:p,"xy"; content:"PCHK";
  0 > "p=xy PCHK"
  1 > "PCHK"

scenario a packet variable is read by a rule written before the one that sets it
> pktvar:q,"zz"; content:"QCHK";
> pcre:"/q=(?P<pkt_q>[a-z]+)/";
  0 > "QCHK q=zz"

scenario a flow variable is read on the packet that sets it by a rule written before
> flowvar:w,"ab"; content:"WCHK";
> pcre:"/w=(?P<flow_w>[a-z]+)/";
  0 > "w=ab WCHK"
  1 > "WCHK"

scenario two captures of one expression
> pcre:"/(?P<flow_k>[a-z]+)=(?P<flow_val>[0-9]+)/";
> flowvar:k,"port"; flowvar:val,"80"; content:"KV";
  0 > "port=80"
  1 > "KV"

scenario a flow variable is read on either side of the flow
> pcre:"/srv=(?P<flow_srv>[a-z]+)/";
< flowvar:srv,"web"; content:"BACKCHK";
  0 > "srv=web"
  1 < "BACKCHK"
